                <pb facs="0633" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10632: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-23T12:00:00+08:00">November 23,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of November 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d487-f1"/>
                    Cantonese authorities have just informed me aeroplanes will bombard Wuchow in
                    the next day or two. I have asked commander of U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mindanao</hi>, now at Wuchow, to advise Americans to leave if possible, but
                    at the same time warned Cantonese authorities time is short and many Americans
                    may not be able to get away, that United States Government will expect every
                    precaution to be taken to avoid harm to Americans and their property and that I
                    could give no assurance as to our attitude in the event of Americans being
                    killed or property damaged. As Cantonese now have 10 or 12 planes, bombing may
                    be serious.</p>
                <p>Legation and Department has been informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
